# Face API conventions

## Stack

- Embeddings: InsightFace `buffalo_l`, `vector(512)` in `face_encoding`
- Device: `FACE_DEVICE=cuda:0` (fallback CPU). Blocking inference goes through `run_on_face_gpu`
- Threshold: `FACE_RECOGNITION_THRESHOLD` (cosine distance; match if `< threshold`)

## Endpoints (do not regress)

| Path | Mode |
|------|------|
| `POST /face/members/{id}/add-face` | enroll |
| `POST /face/members/check-face-emp` | multi-frame + liveness match |
| `POST /face/members/identify` | 1 frame, label only |
| `POST /face/members/check-in` | secure: liveness + timestamp |
| `POST /face/members/check-in-walkby` | 1–2 frames, no motion liveness |
| `WS /face/ws/kiosk` | stream identify/checkin via GPU queue |
| `GET /face/queue-stats` | queue health |

Shared finalize: `_finalize_check_in` (match → company employee → dedupe → photo → timestamp).

## Rules

- Prefer extending `face_controller` / `face_engine` / `face_gpu_queue` over new parallel pipelines
- Walk-by / WS: no head-motion liveness; still require a detectable face (+ same-person if 2+ frames)
- Dedupe: `CHECK_IN_DEDUPE_SECONDS` (default 300) — return `duplicate: true`, do not double-insert
- Outside geofence: `create_timestamp` needs a `note` — kiosk sends a default note
- Nginx: WebSocket needs `^~ /face/ws/` with `Upgrade` headers (see `docker/nginx/default.conf`)
